        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: bocciare",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bocciare — \"to fail (a student); to reject\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Se non studi, ti bocciano. If you do not study, they will fail you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Essere bocciato — to fail a year or an exam. Of a plan: il progetto è stato bocciato."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bocciare is built on boccia \"a ball for bowls\" (EtymDB): first to knock away another player's ball, then to knock out a student. The origin of boccia itself is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
